3DCodeVerse awesome showcase (3DCodeVerse, https://github.com/gaoypeng/3dcodeverse)
  Ported in kit/3dcv/ from the showcase's dataset,
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/3dcodeverse/3dcodeverse-awesome-showcase: six modules of the src/core/ folder in
  its film's code, round r02, which became kit/3dcv/look.js, post.js, paint.js, text.js and util.js (the colour-ramp
  material and its stipple, the post chain, painted textures, stroke lettering, deterministic helpers) and
  kit/3dcv/stage.js (the runtime the shots ran in). Used under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/): credit the creator, no commercial use, adaptations shared
  under the same licence. The files were modified: each has a new header and takes three.js from kit/three.js,
  text.js has neutral default words, and stage.js has film(), a shot adapter for moodreel's stage, in place of the
  page boot. kit/3dcv/LICENSE gives the source of every file and lists the changes file by file. The rest of
  moodreel stays MIT and contains none of this code.
